{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Men who are wise and knowledgeable.</b> Rashi's comment: 'But understanding men I did not find' — this is one of the seven qualities that Jethro told Moses, and he found only three. And if you ask: where are the seven qualities that Jethro told Moses? Are there not only four — 'men of valor, God-fearers, men of truth, haters of unjust gain'? One may answer, this is the explanation: this is one of the seven qualities that Jethro told Moses — for there are four there and three here, making seven between here and there. And thus it is in Eileh HaDevarim Rabbah: Rabbi Berakhiah said in the name of Rabbi Ḥama son of Rabbi Ḥanina: judges need to have seven qualities in them, and these are them — wise, understanding, and knowledgeable, and what is written there — 'And you shall select from all the people men of valor, God-fearers, men of truth, haters of unjust gain' — making seven. And why were all seven not written together in one place? To teach that if they did not find of seven, they bring of four; if they did not find of four, they bring of three — wise, understanding, and knowledgeable; if they did not find of three, they bring of two; if they did not find of two, they bring of one, as it is written: 'A woman of valor, who can find.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {0 "א״ת resolved as ואם תאמר 'and if you ask'; the phrase לא מצאו מד׳ מביאים מג׳ recurs with the abbreviations resolved contextually as מד׳ = מד (four) and מג׳ = מג (three)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:19.609518787Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}